Chapter: E1000Bringup
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

 This test runs the driver against the emulated e1000 in the Device
 Emulation Catalog, so unlike e1000-match it DOES touch registers, both
 descriptor rings and a frame. Its `.vmargs` selects the model and the
 fault, if any.

 What a green result here is evidence of, and it is worth being exact:
 that the driver's own state machine advances and that it survives each
 refusal the model can produce. The model and the driver were written by
 the same agent from the same datasheet reading, so a misreading passes
 both. It is not evidence about silicon, and the hardware sitting stays
 the referee.

 The received frame is reported byte for byte rather than as a count.
 A length alone would be satisfied by any sixty bytes, including sixty
 bytes of uninitialised buffer, and the canned frame carries a broadcast
 destination with an unassigned EtherType precisely so that its bytes
 could not have come from anywhere else.

Section: Fixtures

  bring-up : PciScanResult -> E1000Device
  bring-up (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> e1000-init d
      is None -> e1000-absent

  mk-frame : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  mk-frame (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc else mk-frame (i + 1) n (list-push acc i)

Section: Judges

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  bytes-of : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  bytes-of (l) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else bytes-of l (i + 1) n (acc & " " & show (list-at l i))

  head-of : List Integer, Integer -> Text
  head-of (l) (n) =
    if list-length l < n then "short" else bytes-of l 0 n ""

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let d = bring-up (pci-scan-bus 0)
    in let r = e1000-poll-frame d
    in let frame = r.r-frame
    in let empty = e1000-poll-frame d
    in let sent = e1000-send-frame d (mk-frame 0 64 [])
    in act
      print-line-uni ("present      : " & yn (d.e-present))
      print-line-uni ("mmio in window: " & yn ((d.e-mmio) >= 3221225472 & (d.e-mmio) < 4294967296))
      print-line-uni ("mac valid    : " & yn (d.e-mac-valid))
      print-line-uni ("mac          :" & bytes-of (d.e-mac) 0 (list-length (d.e-mac)) "")
      print-line-uni ("link up      : " & yn (e1000-has-link d))
      print-line-uni ("recv happened: " & yn (r.r-has-frame))
      print-line-uni ("recv length  : " & show (list-length frame))
      print-line-uni ("recv header  :" & head-of frame 14)
      print-line-uni ("second poll  : " & yn (empty.r-has-frame))
      print-line-uni ("send accepted: " & show sent)
    end
  end

